  "limitations": [
    "Blockscout raw traces are provider-returned records; this audit does not independently replay EVM execution.",
    "The raw-trace controller obtains traces through Blockscout's configured execution node, so backend trace availability remains an infrastructure dependency.",
    "The public per-instance Blockscout API is documented but scheduled for deprecation; v2 permits no endpoint substitution after freeze.",
    "The documented flat trace schema does not distinguish CREATE from CREATE2, so both are conservatively normalized as stateful CREATE.",
    "Historical implementation bytecode is hashed but not yet matched to verified source or a reproducible build.",
    "Finality is reported by two provider interfaces; Beacon BLS signatures and Merkle branches are not locally verified.",
    "Governance-neighborhood contamination is limited to the complete frozen D0 Configurator and proxy-log inventory.",
    "No account, participant-action, liquidation, price, oracle or realized-response row is opened, so exposure and causal response remain untested.",
    "V1 failed before any trace result; v2 changes only trace transport, failure evidence and SELFDESTRUCT classification.",
    "The candidate universe is fourteen historical Ethereum mainnet parameter changes and cannot establish cross-market universality."
  ],
